<article class="env-exercise" id="0FWP">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0FWP">Exercise <span data-tag="0FWP">111.62.5</span> <span class="named">(Frobenius)</span>.</a>  Let $p$ be a prime number (you may assume $p = 2$ to simplify the formulas). Let $R$ be a ring such that $p = 0$ in $R$. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
Show that the map $F : R \to R$, $x \mapsto x^ p$ is a ring homomorphism. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
Show that $\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(F) : \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(R) \to \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(R)$ is the identity map. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>